# HAB ST-GNN: Multimodal Spatiotemporal Graph Attention Network for Western Lake Erie Cyanobacterial Bloom Forecasting

Companion codebase for the paper *"A Multimodal Spatiotemporal Graph Attention
Network for Early Warning of Cyanobacterial Harmful Algal Blooms in Western
Lake Erie."*

All scripts are designed to run in **Google Colab** and expect Google Drive
mounted at `/content/drive/MyDrive/hab_stgnn/`. Scripts are numbered in the
order they were developed; not every script needs to be run to reproduce the
paper's final results — see **Minimal Reproduction Path** below.

## Directory Structure

| Folder | Contents |
|---|---|
| `data_acquisition/` | River gage (USGS), lake station (GLERL), and CyAN satellite data pipelines, including the extensive CMR API debugging history (scripts 25-40) |
| `model_training/` | Core ST-GNN architecture development, from early prototypes through the official baseline (script 15) and satellite-integrated model (script 43) |
| `ablation_studies/` | The 11-experiment diagnostic campaign, sequence-length/lead-time ablations, GATv2/ensemble/max-aggregation variants, and the not-yet-executed ViT and fixed-flow-propagation scripts |
| `diagnostics/` | Error analysis, attention inspection, uncertainty quantification, data quality checks |
| `visualization/` | Figure-generating scripts (bloom maps, station maps, Toledo 2014 case study, GAT attention network) |

## Minimal Reproduction Path

To reproduce the paper's primary results without re-running the full
debugging history:

1. `data_acquisition/01_fetch_topology_colab.py` — build the 12-node station graph
2. `data_acquisition/02_fetch_features_colab.py` + `04-05` — river gage features
3. `data_acquisition/07_process_lake_toxin_colab.py` — lake toxin/chlorophyll labels
4. `data_acquisition/35_cyan_production_pipeline_colab.py` or `47_cyan_multiday_average_colab.py` — satellite CI_cyano features (47 is the final, corrected multi-day-averaging version; 35 is an earlier single-day version, kept for history)
5. `model_training/15_official_baseline_colab.py` — tabular-only baseline
6. `model_training/43_satellite_integrated_model_colab.py` — recommended final model
7. `ablation_studies/` — any subset of the 11 diagnostic experiments, run against the locked baseline from step 6

## Known Limitations / Unfinished Work

- `ablation_studies/68_vit_architecture_colab.py` — full training loop is implemented but has not yet been executed; requires patch data from `data_acquisition/47_cyan_multiday_average_colab.py`'s Cell 6 (not yet run)
- `ablation_studies/69_fixed_flow_ablation_colab.py` — has been executed; results reported in paper Section 2.2
- `data_acquisition/70_meteorological_expansion_colab.py` — extended meteorology (temperature/precipitation/humidity) ablation; results reported in paper Table 4, Experiment 11

## Data Sources

See the paper's References section for full citations. Primary sources:
NOAA GLERL/CIGLR, USGS NWIS, NASA/NOAA CyAN, NDBC, Heidelberg University NCWQR.

